on the site of what was once a hatab  home  where 10 members of one family were  killed in an israeli airstrike  artists want to ensure they are not  forgotten  they are painting about life inside  these walls before they were reduced to  rubble  we came today in an initiative called  painting over the rubble  to draw and paint over the homes we want  to deliver a message that no matter what  happens in gaza  and no matter what they do we shall  remain patient and resistant and we  shall have hope for tomorrow  other artists from the gaza strip have  held an exhibition  called we were repainted this  humanitarian scene  sheds light on the fear mixed with  feelings of longing  for those who were killed in the israeli  bombardment  artists are as vulnerable to israeli  attacks  as the refugees in the camps and not all  their work survives  we were preparing for a art exhibition  in ramadan and it was supposed to be  after eid  but then the war happened and our art  atelier was badly destroyed and all our  paintings were destroyed too  this sculpture is one of the art  collections called dignities  that i worked on after the war of 2014  because these 11 days of war brought  back all the sorrows and tragedies that  we lived before  to deliver a message to the world that  we will continue with our art  and with our lives despite all the  tragedies we go through  other sculptures and paintings of people  young and old  embody the feeling of hope dreams as  well  as reality palestinian artists have  chosen to convey messages of peace to  the world  and to remember those who were killed in  the israeli attacks  you may see it al jazeera gaza
 

